  "finding": "**The biology features carry ranking signal beyond attention.** Adding the eight biology features to publication count moves held-out ROC-AUC by +0.054 (95% CI +0.021 to +0.089) and PR-AUC by +0.012 (95% CI +0.001 to +0.025), resampling pairs. The ROC-AUC interval excludes zero under both resampling schemes: resampling whole diseases it is +0.003 to +0.112, with the lower bound close to zero. PR-AUC does not survive that stricter test: resampling diseases, its interval is −0.004 to +0.026, which includes zero. So the ranking improvement is established and the improvement in precision among the rare positives is not. Publication count alone reaches ROC-AUC 0.667; with the biology features, 0.721. The biology features ALONE (M2, ROC-AUC 0.683) do not beat publication count under disease resampling, so they are a useful addition to attention, not a replacement for it.",
